      "problem": "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=-3{b}_{2}$, ${c}_{2}=2{b}_{3}$ and ${c}_{3}=3{b}_{1}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =3{b}_{1}+6{b}_{2}-2{b}_{3} \\\\  & =6{b}_{2}-2{b}_{3}+3{b}_{1} \\\\  & =-2(-3{b}_{2})-2{b}_{3}+3{b}_{1} \\\\  & =-2{c}_{1}-{c}_{2}+{c}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$",
